-- =====================================================================
-- Athlya Platform — initial schema migration (0000_init)
--
-- Generated by `drizzle-kit generate --name init` from the Drizzle schema
-- in `packages/db/src/schema/` and then hand-augmented to:
--   1. Enable the PostgreSQL extensions the schema relies on
--      (`pgcrypto` for `gen_random_uuid()`, `citext` for case-insensitive
--      emails). Requirement 22.2 and the data-model section of design.md.
--   2. Rewrite `users.email` as `citext` so `UNIQUE(email)` is
--      case-insensitive by construction.
--   3. Install an `audit_log_immutable()` trigger that forbids UPDATE and
--      DELETE on `audit_log`, giving the append-only guarantee required
--      by Requirement 22.2 at the SQL layer (RLS policies in migration
--      0001 add a second line of defence).
--
-- All extension and function statements use `IF NOT EXISTS` /
-- `CREATE OR REPLACE` so this migration is safely re-runnable against a
-- database that partially applied it.
--
-- NOTE (UUID v7): `gen_random_uuid()` from `pgcrypto` generates UUID v4.
-- Neon does not yet ship `pg_uuidv7` as a managed extension (checked
-- 2026-Q1 Neon docs). When `pg_uuidv7` becomes available, a follow-up
-- migration should:
--   1. `CREATE EXTENSION IF NOT EXISTS "pg_uuidv7";`
--   2. `ALTER TABLE <each> ALTER COLUMN id SET DEFAULT uuid_generate_v7();`
--   3. Flip `DEFAULT_UUID_SQL` in `packages/db/src/schema/_shared.ts`.
-- Until then, UUID v4 is a correct (though slightly less
-- index-locality-friendly) drop-in.
-- =====================================================================

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------
-- 1. Extensions
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------

CREATE EXTENSION IF NOT EXISTS "pgcrypto";--> statement-breakpoint
CREATE EXTENSION IF NOT EXISTS "citext";--> statement-breakpoint

-- TODO(uuid-v7): enable `pg_uuidv7` once Neon exposes it as a managed
-- extension and swap every `id uuid DEFAULT gen_random_uuid()` to
-- `DEFAULT uuid_generate_v7()`. Tracked alongside task 2.2.
-- CREATE EXTENSION IF NOT EXISTS "pg_uuidv7";

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------
